<title>BELGIUM: EU sets peripheral territory food supply aids.</title>
<headline>EU sets peripheral territory food supply aids.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aid for the supply of food to peripheral regions of the European Union for March was set by last week's cereals and rice management committee, said a note in the EU official journal received on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The announcement, dated March 1, gave aid for supplies of cereals products to French overseas departments in Ecus per tonne as:</p>
<p>		    Guadaloupe  Martinique French Reunion  Guyana</p>
<p> Common wheat     19.00     19.00	   19.00	    22.00</p>
<p> Barley	     33.50     33.50	   33.50	    36.50</p>
<p> Maize		39.00     39.00	   39.00	    42.00</p>
<p> Durum wheat	12.00     12.00	   12.00	    16.00</p>
<p>For cereals products to the Canary Islands (Ecus per tonne):</p>
<p> Common wheat     16.00</p>
<p> Barley	     30.50</p>
<p> Maize		36.00</p>
<p> Durum wheat	 9.00</p>
<p> Oats		 33.00</p>
<p>For cereals products to the Azores and Madeira (Ecus per tonne):</p>
<p>			Azores    Madeira</p>
<p> Common wheat     16.00     16.00</p>
<p> Barley	     30.50     30.50</p>
<p> Maize		36.00     36.00</p>
<p> Durum wheat	 9.00	9.00</p>
<p>Aid rates for the supply of rice products to the Canary Islands (Ecus per tonne):</p>
<p> Milled rice     260.00</p>
<p> Broken rice	57.00</p>
<p>Aid for the supply of rice products to the Azores and Madeira (Ecus per tonne):</p>
<p>		     Azores     Madeira</p>
<p> Milled rice     260.00     260.00</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
